  worker_seed = torch.initial_seed() % 2**32 #Here % is the modulo operator（求余数）. Because torch.initial_seed() can be a very large integer, but NumPy’s random seed must fit into a smaller range, usually from: 0 to 2**32 - 1/.So this line converts the PyTorch seed into a valid NumPy/Python random seed.
  numpy.random.seed(worker_seed)
  random.seed(worker_seed)


